{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 17, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.2-3b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III was the last ruler of the County of Tripoli a Crusader state in the Middle East from 1152 until his death in 1187. He succeeded his brother Peter as count at the age of 14 and took control of the county through a series of military campaigns against the Zengid dynasty.\n\n**Early Life and Reign Part 1**\nRaymond III was born around 1140 to Raymond II Count of Tripoli and his second wife Alp Arslan's daughter Adelaida. Raymond II died when Raymond III was 14 years old and he became the count of Tripoli. Raymond III married Constance of Antioch and had three sons including Raymond IV Count of Tripoli.\n\n**Military Campaigns and Alliances Part 2**\nRaymond III expanded the county through military campaigns against the Zengid dynasty and established alliances with the Kingdom of Jerusalem and the Kingdom of Cyprus. He also fought against the Fatimid Caliphate. In 1157 Raymond III led a campaign against the Zengid forces in Syria and in 1167 he led another campaign to recapture the city of Aleppo. Raymond III also fought against Saladin in the Battle of Montgisard in 1177.\n\n**Death and Legacy Part 3**\nRaymond III died in 1187 during the Third Crusade. He was killed in the Siege of Hattin. Raymond III's death led to the fall of the County of Tripoli to the Ayyubid dynasty. Raymond III's legacy is remembered as a skilled military leader who expanded the county through a series of military campaigns. He also established alliances with other Crusader states and fought against the Zengid dynasty and the Fatimid Caliphate.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.001581966644152999}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.0001299296854995191}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -1.9862117767333984}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.4664328396320343}, {"token": " last", "logprob": -1.3259131908416748}, 